From: RNSBox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: sophgo: reclock the EVB UARTs for exact 2 Mbaud

clk_cam0_200 was still on the 25 MHz crystal: the DTS asked for 96 MHz
but no parent produced it. Set disppll to 768 MHz first (the vendor LUT
row added by the previous patch) and then clk_cam0_200 to disppll/8:
2 Mbaud becomes exact (96 MHz / 16 / 3) and the 115200 console lands on
divisor 52 (+0.16%).

The parents array is positional, so disppll itself gets <0> (no change)
and cam0_200 gets disppll. The parent switch needs the bypass-mux fix:
without it the mux field stayed on the crystal.

--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-duomodule01-evb.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-duomodule01-evb.dts
@@ -304,9 +304,9 @@
  * this mux in a state Linux can rely on, so pin parent and rate here.
  */
 &clk {
-	assigned-clocks = <&clk CLK_CAM0_200>;
-	assigned-clock-parents = <&clk CLK_DISPPLL>;
-	assigned-clock-rates = <96000000>;
+	assigned-clocks = <&clk CLK_DISPPLL>, <&clk CLK_CAM0_200>;
+	assigned-clock-parents = <0>, <&clk CLK_DISPPLL>;
+	assigned-clock-rates = <768000000>, <96000000>;
 };
 
